[19.694, "o", "_Imported from Conductor by `conch import conductor`._\r\n\r\n# Handoff: Add coupon codes to checkout\r\n\r\nConversation from a Claude Code session (`0199f1c2-3a10-7b4e-9c21-4f8a2d6e1b01`) in `~/conductor/workspaces/storefront/lisbon` on branch `ada/coupon-codes`, 2026-11-02 10:14 – 2026-11-02 11:02.\r\n\r\nOnly the messages are included: tool calls, command output and file edits are left out, so check the files themselves for the current state.\r\n\r\n## User · 2026-11-02 10:14:00\r\n\r\nAdd coupon codes to checkout. A code takes a percentage or a fixed amount off the cart; codes have an expiry date and a usage limit. Store them in Postgres next to orders.\r\n\r\n## Claude Code · 2026-11-02 10:16:00\r\n\r\nI'll look at how checkout totals are computed first.\r\n\r\nPlan:\r\n\r\n1. A `coupons` table (code, kind, amount, expires_at, max_uses, uses).\r\n2. `applyCoupon(cart, code)` in `app/checkout/coupon.ts`, returning the discount or why it was refused.\r\n3. A field on the"]
[19.694, "o", " checkout page, and the discount as a line in the summary.\r\n\r\nI've written the migration and `applyCoupon`; the page is next.\r\n\r\n## User · 2026-11-02 10:22:00\r\n\r\nFixed-amount coupons must never take the total below zero. And show the reason when a code is refused.\r\n\r\n## Claude Code · 2026-11-02 10:24:00\r\n\r\nDone: the discount is capped at the cart's subtotal, and a refused code says why under the field (*expired*, *used up*, *not a code*). Still to do: an admin page to create codes — for now they're inserted with `pnpm coupons:add`.\r\n"]
